hw/sh4: ze0-gfx QMP input forwarding to the panel peer (TODO M8.H40).

The M8.H4 console has no QemuInputHandler, so QMP input-send-event fails
with "Input handler not found". Register a handler bound to ze0-gfx that
forwards abs/btn/key events as text commands on a chardev; the panel peer
replays them over the same SCI3 display-unit link M8.H39 used.

Machine option gfx-input=ID names the chardev; gfx-display=off leaves the
console (and handler) absent, the negative control.

